sauvegarde.description:
All of Vision's configuration: roles, people, devices and their rules, modules, place, widgets, screensaver. The files stay in Home Assistant (folder “vision_sauvegardes” in the configuration) and are included in its own backups. An automatic backup is made every night.

Available backups:
{liste}

sauvegarde_creer.description:
Saves Vision's current configuration. The last 20 backups made here are kept.

Already there:
{liste}

temps_gagne.description:
A task ticked in a Home Assistant to-do list gives extra time on the person's devices. Tasks already ticked when you set this up do not count, and a task unticked then ticked again only counts once. Leave the list empty to remove a person's setting.

Current settings:
{resume}

regles_lieu.description:
While the person is in the chosen zone (based on their location in Home Assistant), the ticked categories are blocked on their devices. When they leave the zone, everything goes back to how it was. Tick no category to remove this person's rule for this zone.

Current rules:
{resume}

soutien.description:
Vision is free and open source. If you'd like to thank the project, you can buy it a coffee: {lien}

In return, a "Supporter" badge appears and the Vision eye occasionally winks, with a small heart, on the screensaver and in "About". It is purely decorative: no feature is locked.

The code you receive by e-mail is checked here, offline: nothing is sent anywhere.

code_gestion.description:
{etat}

This code releases, on a PC, a message that blocks “until released”. It can only be set here (administrators): the Vision window on the PC can no longer choose it. Home Assistant keeps only its fingerprint and checks it itself; the PC keeps nothing. After {essais} wrong codes on a PC, its tries are paused for {minutes} minutes; after {total} wrong codes in 24 h across the whole place, the code is locked until it is changed here.

6 to 32 characters. A code typed on a PC goes through the Requester's session: do not type it in front of them, and change it if in doubt. A blocking message can also be released from Home Assistant (“Release a message” action), without a code.
